<heading>grants group add - Grant a permission to a group.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  add NAME PATH
  add NAME PATH --bits rwx
  add NAME PATH --deny
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Grants a permission to a group. All members of the group
inherit this permission. Use --bits to control read/write/
execute access and --deny to explicitly forbid an action.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
add admins /usr/bin --bits rwx
  Grant full /usr/bin access to the admins group.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
group/show, group/remove, account/add, path/show
</paragraph>
